{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"rent_increase_limits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Berkeley Rent Ordinance annual general adjustment cap (Measure BB)","requirement":"The annual general adjustment that sets how much a landlord of a fully covered unit may raise rent is capped at a maximum of 5%, even if the Rent Ordinance formula yields more. Landlords may only petition for increases for completed capital improvements.","key_value":"5% maximum AGA per year","coverage_conditions":"Fully covered rental units, including most multifamily units built before 1980; government-owned or subsidized units are now fully or partially covered. Units with a certificate of occupancy issued after 1980 are only partially covered.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"built","role":"exempt","op":"after","date":"1980","basis":"certificate_of_occupancy"},{"type":"other","text":"government-owned or -subsidized units are fully or partially covered depending on unit type and whether other law prohibits rent control"},{"type":"owner","role":"exempt","who":"landlord lived on the same property at the start of the tenancy","unit_limit":null}],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":["The AGA is the amount by which the landlord of a fully-covered rental unit may raise the rent each year.","New Construction Units (units with a certificate of occupancy issued after 1980)","Where the tenant shares a kitchen or bath facilities with the landlord, the unit will be exempt from the Rent Ordinance only if the landlord lived in a unit on the same property at the start of the tenancy."]},"exemptions":"New construction units certified for occupancy after 1980, most single-family homes and most condominiums are only partially covered; shared kitchen or bath units unless the landlord lived on the property; banked unused AGAs may raise rent above 5%.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"Berkeley Mun. Code ch. 13.76","quoted_span":"The maximum AGA is 5%. This means that, if the formula in the Rent Ordinance results in an AGA that is greater than 5%, the AGA approved by the Board for that year can be no more than 5%.","interaction":"Units are only partially covered where Federal law, State law, or administrative regulation prohibits rent control under the Ordinance.","relations":[],"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Berkeley Rent Ordinance just cause eviction changes (Measure BB)","requirement":"A landlord of a fully or partially covered unit may evict only for just cause. Nonpayment eviction requires rental debt of at least one month's Fair Market Rent, and lease-breach evictions are allowed only for substantial, actual harm.","key_value":"1 month's FMR minimum rental debt","coverage_conditions":"Tenants in units fully or partially covered by the Rent Ordinance, including government-owned or subsidized units now covered. Units sharing kitchen or bath with a landlord who lived on the property are exempt.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"other","text":"government-owned or -subsidized units are now fully or partially covered"},{"type":"owner","role":"exempt","who":"landlord lived on the same property at the start of the tenancy","unit_limit":null}],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":["Government-owned or -subsidized rental units become either fully or partially covered by the Rent Ordinance.","Where the tenant shares a kitchen or bath facilities with the landlord, the unit will be exempt from the Rent Ordinance only if the landlord lived in a unit on the same property at the start of the tenancy."]},"exemptions":"Units sharing a kitchen or bath with the landlord, unless the landlord lived in a unit on the same property at the start of the tenancy.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"Berkeley Mun. Code ch. 13.76","quoted_span":"For a landlord to evict a tenant for nonpayment of rent, the tenant must owe an amount of rental debt equal to or greater than one month of the Fair Market Rent (FMR) value for a unit of equivalent size in the metro area Oakland-Fremont, CA HUD Metro FMR as determined by the US Department of Housing and Urban Development for the fiscal year in which the rent is demanded.","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
